  "implementation": [
    "Maintained selected F64 matrix add/subtract/multiply/divide now operate directly on current exact Core F64 banks. Scalar, row, column and exact broadcasting use the already validated geometry. The operation is matched once outside the loop, removing generic operand/result ValueDataDraft construction and per-cell operation dispatch.",
    "The resident/JIT compiler execution path is shared. Both current schema/backing pairs must be exact F64 and the result must be a matrix with exact F64 schema. Dense column-major transport, other numeric kinds, constrained/composite schemas, power/remainder and rational power keep their existing paths.",
    "The original complete preflight runs before typed selection. Source input/schema/shape and full length checks, output/clone/temporary/node/compute/comparison/storage envelopes, strict Core typed construction, prior-output publication comparison and atomic replacement are unchanged. No source arithmetic reassociation, FMA, result cache, cached pointer or admission capability is introduced.",
    "IR377/work146 identify the execution change; all existing numeric source/construction prices and both exact Huffman work equations remain unchanged. No benchmark source, input, pinned C binary, tolerance or timing boundary changed."
  ],
